A||||6||Neal||Cloyes timing chain instal ?||||5||
Z||000000||Neal||10-28-2001||03:37 PM||||When installing the cloyes true roller timing chain there is no room for the "chain guide" (ya know the triangle piece that fits inside the chain and gears).  Should this piece be left out, only problem i see with this is the bolt holes that hold the unit on go right through to the main block.<P>i was thinking put the bolts in to plug the holes and leave it at that.<BR>Anyone who has a cloyes PLEASE help me out.<P>neal||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||10-28-2001||04:05 PM||||You're not supposed to use the timing chain guide with a Cloyes roller timing chain. I says so in the instructions!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 10-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Neal||10-28-2001||05:47 PM||||Doh, it does to.  But the holes for the bolts still go through into the main block.  Plug em or leave em?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||10-28-2001||08:34 PM||||I think when I rebuilt my 3.4 I didn't put the bolts back in. I don't think there is any reason to since the only thing that is going to come through there is oil splashed from the reciprocating assembly and that is good. If you put the bolts in and they happen to come loose they could do some serious damage!||||reg||1
Z||000004||DreXteR||10-29-2001||12:59 PM||||Does the cloys roller time chain will geve some hp?<P>thanx<P>DreX<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://users.centennialpr.net/drexter/fierofire1.jpg">        <BR>  <BR>Just another Red Fiero - Back 2 the Future Prototype. :D||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT GT 87||10-29-2001||05:48 PM|||| They are supposed to add 2-3 Hp. I put one in my 3.2., It's not finished yet........||||reg||1
Z||000006||Neal||10-29-2001||07:56 PM||||hmm i would highly doubt any power increase that would be noticable.  MAYBE on a dyno but if your going to put one in do it for the durability/reliability factor.<P>Of that im not totaly impressed with the cloyes unit, the bushings in the chain are just rolled peices not a solid piece, like you SHOULD find on a quality roller chain.<BR>But it sure as hell is better quality than the OEM part||||reg||1
